#- §5╔═.✵.════════╗  §2    ᴡʜɪᴛᴇ ᴡᴇᴅᴅɪɴɢ...
§5╚════════.✵.═╝

§2In the heart of an Enchanted Forest, where snowflakes danced in the wintry air and the trees whispered ancient secrets, a magical winter wedding was about to take place.§r
#- §2Fern, stood beneath 
a grand arch woven from interlacing vines, her petals shimmering with an ethereal glow. 

Beside her, in regal attire adorned with glistening crystals, stood Castien. The Elf mage prince, his eyes reflecting the love he felt for Fern after so many adventures.§r
#- §2The ceremony was a blend of nature’s wonders and elven enchantment. Ice sculptures shaped like blooming roses adorned the surroundings, and a gentle snowfall added a touch of magic to the air. As the vows were about to be exchanged, a hush fell over the§r
#- §2assembly. Fern’s mother, Marigold, a powerful witch with a complex past, stepped forward with a stern expression on her face.§r 

§6“I object to this marriage,”§r §2she declared, her voice echoing. Gasps of surprise rippled through the crowd.§r
#- §2Castien stood protectively by Fern's side, his eyes meeting Marigold’s. “Why, Mother?” Fern asked, her voice soft.§r 

§2Marigold hesitated, her eyes softening for a moment before hardening once more.§r §6“I fear for your heart, my dear Fern,”§r §2she said, her voice§r
#- §2carrying the weight of sorrow.§6 "Love between different worlds is fragile, and I worry that it will bring you nothing but pain.” §2Castien stepped forward, his voice steady yet filled with empathy. §c“But love knows no boundaries, no constraints. It blossoms where it will, through time itself!"§r
#- §2The forest around them seemed to hold its breath, awaiting Marigold’s response. After a moment of contemplation, her expression softened, and she sighed, her eyes filling with tears.§r 
§6“I see the sincerity in your eyes, both of you,”§r §2she said, her voice gentle now.§r
#- §6“If my Fern’s heart has chosen you, Castien, then who am I to stand in the way of fate?”§r §2With those words, the tension lifted. Fern and Castien exchanged their vows, promising eternal love and devotion. As they kissed, the forest burst into a symphony of colours...§r
#- §2flowers blooming in vibrant hues and the snowflakes transforming into tiny, shimmering stars. 
They knew their love was strong enough to overcome any obstacle, even the doubts of a once-wary mother.§r

§5How do you know what the wedding was like?§r
#- §6Two words: 
Automatic Writing!§r

§5Ah.. trying that trick again, even after what happened last time... 
I’m impressed.§r

§6Oh, And I was there.§r
§5O.o WHAT!?§r

§6How else was I 
meant to give them 
a wedding gift ;)
#- §2With the wedding celebrations in full swing, Fern and Castien found a quiet moment to explore the array of enchanting gifts bestowed upon them. Among the carefully wrapped packages, Fern’s 
eyes fell upon a suspiciously elegant box, labeled...§r
§6'From Sweetpea'.§r
#- §2Excited but cautious, Fern delicately unwrapped it, revealing a heart-shaped necklace crafted from brilliant purple amethyst, with a tiny teardrop-shaped glass gem nestled beneath. The moment Fern touched the necklace, she felt a gentle warmth.§r
#- §2She lifted the necklace, allowing the light to catch it, creating a dazzling display. Castien watched, captivated.§r
§2“Sweetpea has a heart as beautiful as this gem, I only wish she knew that,” Fern murmured, her voice filled with wonder.
As she admired the necklace, the glass§r
#- §2teardrop caught her attention. It seemed to shimmer with an ethereal light, almost as if it held a secret.

Fern gently touched the glass, and suddenly, a vision washed over her, a glimpse of a distant future, whole other lifetimes, shrouded in a dark mystery...§r
#- §c“What do you see?”§r §2Castien asked, his elven senses attuned to the magical energies around them.

Fern blinked, returning from the vision. “I saw a strange island, bathed in moonlight, people lost and found again... pieces of someone else’s story, Castien.”§r
#- §2Castien’s eyes widened with intrigue.§r §c“A shared memory, perhaps? How extraordinary.”§r
§2With the necklace clasped around her neck, Fern felt a deep connection to Sweetpea. It was as though they were bound by an unseen thread, woven 
through time.§r
#- §2“I will treasure this gift always,” Fern whispered, her voice filled with gratitude. Out the corner of her eye, Fern saw the last trace of Sweetpea fade in the soft glow of the winter evening with a smile.
 
“And I will carry these stories and memories with me..."
#- §5The heart necklace??§r
§6Yeah! Cool right? Simple yet elegant.§r
§5How did you do that?§r
§6Time travel via 
magic obviously! 
I thought she’d like it...§r
§5Okay you are getting more powerful 
by the second.§r
§6Gift wrapped too! 
Such a nice wedding.§r
§6Now we are connected!§r
§6Through time...§r
#- §5Wait the heart necklace she has in all the title pages of ‘ferns adventures’ is because it was a gift she got from you… this whole time, 
THE WHOLE TIME!?§r
§6What’s the problem?§r
§5Umm.. nothing, forget it.§r
§6You sound like you know this necklace...§r
§5It's fine forget it.§r
§6Okay then, I will...§r
#- §2To be continued??
