§8A Note About Society:
Written by: Unknown
Edited by: Unknown§r
§c-------------------§r
§7P.S: I found out my previous work was featured in a "deluxe"§r
#- §7Society, it is what you and I are in. But is it ran properly? Is there such a thing as a "perfect society"? 

There are many questions which must be answered when creating a society.

Many have different beliefs on how society should be ran.§r
#- §7Some believe it is best if things are owned privately. 

Others believe it is best if everyone owns everything.

John Rawls once argued that the perfect society is created when we don't know our identity, abilities, social status...§r 
#- §7or personal
circumstances. 

This is because we as humans are biased. 

When making a society we make it based off our needs and class.

A poor person might design a society where everyone is equal in wealth.§r
#- §7A rich person might design a society where they stay rich.

Now there are also many questions raised when creating a "perfect society".

What happens to those who commit crimes?
How do you keep people at bay and stop war?§r
#- §7How do you keep people in power from getting greedy?

How do you make everyone equal?§r
§c-------------------§r
§5I don't know who sends these in, but they are smart.§r
§6How to make the "perfect society"?
§0Reset it all... ☠
